engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript)

// `RootEntity` exposes public setters for `id`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`.
// They exist so MikroORM's `accessor: true` mapping can hydrate private backing
// fields without `@ts-expect-error`, which `ddd/users-api/README.md` documents as
// a deliberate trade-off for this sample.
//
// The cost of that trade-off is that aggregate identity is assignable from
// anywhere. Removing the setters would mean introducing persistence records and
// explicit mappers — worthwhile only if strict domain encapsulation becomes a
// goal of the sample, which the consolidating review concluded it is not. Until
// then the setters stay and this rule carries the other half of the bargain:
// application and presentation code must go through factories and domain
// methods.
//
// Scoped in biome.json to the layers that must not assign identity. The
// persistence and domain trees are excluded: the ORM hydrates through these
// setters, and the aggregate itself owns its timestamps via `onUpdate()`.

`$aggregate.$property = $value` as $assignment where {
  $property <: r"^(?:id|createdAt|updatedAt)$",
  register_diagnostic(span=$assignment, message="Do not assign aggregate identity or lifecycle timestamps. These setters exist only for MikroORM hydration; application code creates aggregates through factories (User.create) and changes them through domain methods (user.update), which maintain the version and updatedAt invariants.", severity="error")
}
